 "substitutedBy": null,
 "summary": "Authorizes the commissioner of health to make grants to not-for-profit organizations and elementary, secondary and postsecondary schools to be used to help pay for the costs of conducting local blood drives.",
 "title": "Authorizes the commissioner of health to make grants to be used to help pay for the costs of conducting local blood drives",
 "vetoMessages": {
  "items": [
   {
    "billId": {
     "basePrintNo": "A375",
     "basePrintNoStr": "A375-2015",
     "printNo": "A375",
     "session": 2015,
     "version": ""
    },
    "billPage": 0,
    "chapter": 0,
    "lineEnd": 0,
    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 188\n\nTO THE ASSEMBLY:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nAssembly Bill Number 375, entitled:\n\n    \"AN  ACT  to amend the public health law, in relation to authorizing\n      the commissioner of health to make grants to be used for the costs\n      of conducting a local blood donation drive\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would authorize the funding of grants to  non-profit  organ-\nizations and schools to help pay for the costs of conducting local blood\ndonation  drives.  The  Department  of  Health  (DOH) currently supports\nappeals for increased donation during seasonal or weather-related short-\nages, and also works with other agencies  to  distribute  mailings  that\nencourage  blood  donation  and  provide  contact  information for blood\ncenters. DOH also collects data on behalf of blood banks on  the  number\nof  units of blood collected and transfused, and provides administrative\nand technical support to the New York State Council on Human  Blood  and\nTransfusion  Services,  which is charged with maximizing blood safety in\nNew York.\n\n  While I fully support the intent of this  bill,  it  would  result  in\nincreased  and  unbudgeted costs to the DOH, and for that reason, should\nnecessarily be addressed in the context of enacting  the  overall  State\nbudget.  Accordingly,  while I am constrained to disapprove this bill, I\nwill direct DOH to continue its ongoing efforts to encourage and support\nlocal blood donation across the State.  I also encourage all New Yorkers\nwho are eligible to donate to do so, and further acknowledge and commend\nthe efforts of volunteers throughout the State who work  with  organiza-\ntions that sponsor local blood drives.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
    "vetoNumber": 188,
    "vetoType": "STANDARD",
    "year": 2015
   }
